#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""agent-resume: resume a Claude Code teammate in its swarm tmux session.

--into-team TEAM|live relaunches an agent under the destination team identity,
stops any process holding the transcript, registers the destination roster
entry, and retires the source entry. Lead migration moves the lead alone and
reports the members that retain their existing team. The team component of an
agent ID addresses an identity; --into-team selects a destination.

--into-session selects the parent embedded by demotion. --as-agent selects the
identity used by promotion. --team selects the agents operated on.

--install creates the ~/.local/bin symlink, installs zsh completion, and adds the
Claude Code startup hook that runs --cleanup.

A bare selector can be replaced with --agent-id and/or --resume <session-uuid>.
The tool reconstructs team, type, color, model, effort, permission mode, cwd,
parent session, tmux socket, and pane from disk records and live processes.
Dated observations use newest-first precedence; explicit identity assignment and
promotion receipts remain authoritative until an intentional move replaces them.

Resumed-session flags can appear beside tool flags. An explicit forwarded flag
overrides the derived value. Unknown flags are reported with the nearest match
before Claude Code starts.
"""

